  "flowText": "# VIII. Grading System and Retention Policies\n## A. Graduate Studies Grading System\n    The grading system for the master's degree observes the\nnumerical system. The numerical system is described to indicate the\nfollowing:\n|Number|Percent|Descriptive|\n|1.00|99-100|Excellent|\n|1.25|96-98|Very Good|\n|1.50|93-95|Very Good|\n|1.75|90-92|Good|\n|2.00|87-89|Good|\n|2.25|84-86|Fair|\n|2.50|81-83|Fair|\n|2.75|78-80|Fair|\n|3.00|75-77|Passing|\n|5.00|70|Failed|\n|Inc||Incomplete|\n|uw/70||Unauthorized Withdrawal|\n|w|-|Withdrawn|\n\n## B. College Grading System in All Departments\n    The work of students in the Collegiate Department will be graded at\n the end of each term, semester, or summer in accordance with the\nfollowing system.\n|Percent|Number|Descriptive|\n|99-100|(1.00)|Excellent|\n|96-98|(1.25)|Very Good|\n|93-95|(1.50)|Very Good|\n|90-92|(1.75)|Good|\n|87-89|(2.00)|Good|\n|84-86|(2.25)|Fair|\n|81-83|(2.50)|Fair|\n|78-80|(2.75)|Fair|\n|75-77|(3.00)|Passing|\n|70|(5.00)|Failed|\n|Inc|(inc.)|Incomplete|\n|uw/70|uw/70|Unauthorized Withdrawal|\n|W|-|Withdrawn|\n\n## BSN Grading System\n    To attain high standards of student performance in preparation for\nboard examinations, the Nursing Department in all its major subjects\nshall observe a base grade of 40."
}
